WEBVTT

00:00:00.639 --> 00:00:05.050
Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification, commonly called CMMC 2.0,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.760
is the Department of Defense program for verifying that defense contractors implement

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.715
required safeguards for sensitive unclassified information.

00:00:11.715 --> 00:00:15.324
The program applies within the Defense Industrial Base, or DIB:

00:00:15.324 --> 00:00:19.625
the large ecosystem of prime contractors, subcontractors, suppliers, service providers,

00:00:19.625 --> 00:00:23.425
and other organizations that support Department of Defense missions and contracts.

00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:26.725
CMMC focuses on Federal Contract Information, known as FCI,

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:30.100
and Controlled Unclassified Information, known as CUI.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.720
The information an organization receives, creates, stores, processes,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.720
or transmits helps determine which requirements may apply.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.070
The program uses three levels that correspond to increasing information sensitivity and

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.515
cybersecurity expectations.

00:00:42.515 --> 00:00:46.520
It also uses assessment and affirmation mechanisms to provide confidence that required

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.080
practices are implemented.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.730
CMMC does not replace every other contract clause, security obligation,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.995
or risk-management activity.

00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:57.640
Organizations remain responsible for reading the applicable solicitation and contract,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.988
understanding information flows, and satisfying all relevant requirements.

00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:04.630
A CMMC status is not simply a security product or document.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:08.645
It depends on people, processes, technology, governance, defined scope, evidence,

00:01:08.645 --> 00:01:12.615
and sustained operation across the environment that handles protected information.

00:01:12.615 --> 00:01:15.185
CMMC affects more than compliance staff.

00:01:15.185 --> 00:01:19.300
Executives, contract teams, engineers, administrators, developers, employees,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.545
and suppliers all influence whether information is handled within approved systems and

00:01:23.545 --> 00:01:24.705
protected as required.

00:01:24.705 --> 00:01:29.120
This course provides educational information about CMMC 2.0 concepts.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.510
It is not legal advice, compliance consulting, audit guidance, assessment preparation,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.645
or certification advice.

00:01:35.645 --> 00:01:39.595
Contract-specific questions require current official sources and qualified counsel or

00:01:39.595 --> 00:01:39.900
advisors.
